; `any` as a bare type-choice arm (`any / tstr`) is a GRACEFUL rejection in EVERY profile: `any`
; overlaps every other CBOR type, so a catch-all union arm needs forced-backtracking dispatch
; (loose-CBOR phase A3). A2 rejects it with a message naming the supported positions (member /
; array / table / tagged / top-level). Formerly panicked at an `Option::unwrap()` in
; intermediate/rust_type.rs. A CONTAINER-of-any arm (`[* any] / tstr`,
; tests/robustness/choice_array_any_arm.cddl) is supported instead. Surfaced by the recombination
; sweep (src/tests/recombination_tests.rs).
a = any / tstr
